WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.680 --> 00:00:04.280
So how did you feel about that initially?

2
00:00:04.280 --> 00:00:06.600
Finding out that you were a descendant?

3
00:00:06.600 --> 00:00:14.200
I was happy, because most black people . . . I mean, you can’t get past 1895, and here we are, 1770.

4
00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:15.540
What!

5
00:00:15.540 --> 00:00:19.300
You have a paper trail, which most of us . . . we don’t have a paper trail.

6
00:00:19.300 --> 00:00:21.200
You just hear stories.

7
00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:23.040
So here I am, a black person.

8
00:00:23.040 --> 00:00:25.100
Black black.

9
00:00:25.100 --> 00:00:25.680
Here I am.

10
00:00:25.680 --> 00:00:29.100
I have my ancestry dating to the American Revolution.

11
00:00:29.100 --> 00:00:35.740
That was the most exciting thing ever, because I used to tell my white friends, “I’m more American than you!

12
00:00:35.740 --> 00:00:38.300
Your family came in the 1800s and I was already here.”

13
00:00:38.300 --> 00:00:38.680
You know.

14
00:00:38.680 --> 00:00:42.760
It’s like a sense of . . . I wouldn’t know exactly what part of Africa I’m from,

15
00:00:42.760 --> 00:00:48.260
but I’m past that hurdle that most blacks can’t make, that connection with that one slave.

16
00:00:48.260 --> 00:00:49.280
And here I am.

17
00:00:49.280 --> 00:00:52.760
It’s just so many of them.

18
00:00:52.760 --> 00:00:54.090
It’s like ecstatic.
